 - the layout is exposed by the `C`, `Fortran` and `Python` bindings.
 
-The functions of the material data managers no longer allocate memory on
-the heap at each call in the usual cases, nor `evaluate`.
+Once the arrays are allocated, the synchronous functions processing
+points (integration, initialize functions, post-processings, rotations,
+`evaluate`) and `update` and `revert` no longer allocate memory on the
+heap in the calling thread, for the material data managers and for the
+views. This is checked by a test.
+
+# Bug fixes
+
+- Copying a `RotationMatrix2D` or a `RotationMatrix3D` outside of `MGIS`
+  failed to link (`MaterialAxisStorage` was not exported), and the copy
+  of a material axis stored locally referred to the values of the
+  original.
+- The `Fortran` function `material_data_manager_get_tangent_operator`
+  returned an array whose first extent was not set.
+- The `Python` bindings read a strided `numpy` array given as an array of
+  values (for instance `a[::2]`) as a contiguous one: it is now refused.
 
