 A uniform view (null point stride) can only be read. The values of an
-output must be distinct: `MGIS` checks it (`hasDistinctValues`).
+output must be distinct: `MGIS` checks it (`hasDistinctValues`). Two
+different outputs of a function must not overlap: this is not checked.
+
+A view is trivially copyable: it can be copied to the memory of a device
+and used by the kernels of the calling code. Its member functions are
+`constexpr`: with `nvcc`, they can be called in device code with the
+`--expt-relaxed-constexpr` option.
+
+The views of `mgis::function` stored point by point (`FunctionView`) or
+with a strided coalesced memory access can be converted to `FieldView` by
+the `mgis::function::makeFieldView` functions
+(`MGIS/Function/FieldViewSupport.hxx`). The conversions follow the
+constness of the views of `mgis::function`.
 
