@@ -137,6 +155,18 @@ variable by variable, in the order of the behaviour, by
 Each one is uniform or given at each point. The vectors holding those
 views use a memory resource given to the constructor.
 
+The view keeps a pointer to its behaviour, which must outlive the view (a
+view can't be built for a temporary behaviour). The members are public:
+the copies of a view copy descriptors, never values. The outputs of a view
+(thermodynamic forces, internal state variables, energies, tangent
+operator blocks, speed of sound) must not overlap each other.
+
+The computation of the speed of sound requires the mass density at the
+beginning and at the end of the time step for a behaviour generated by the
+`generic-parallel` interface. For the other behaviours, a missing mass
+density is null, as for the material data managers. The tangent operator
+blocks of a point where the integration failed are unspecified.
+
